10.0 Conclusion

The Level 2 Quiz Management System successfully demonstrates the use of C programming concepts such as structures, file handling, loops, and conditional statements to build a functional multi-user application.

The system simulates a basic learning management system and introduces real-world software development concepts such as authentication, data persistence, and modular programming.

This project provides a strong foundation for understanding how educational software systems are designed and implemented.

